nsing by physicians currently helps\nmillions of patients around the country.\n\nUnfortunately, New York State law has failed to similarly keep pace\nwith medical developments, and New York is one of only three states in\nthe nation that prohibits the dispensing of medications by physicians.\nThis has resulted in certain medications not being as accessible to\nNew York patients as they are in other states, thus keeping some\npatients away from desired treatments and driving others out of state\nto obtain treatment.\n\nTo address this, this bill would allow consumers to access, in a\ndoctor's office setting, certain identified pharmaceuticals that are\ndispensed only to change physical appearance if a doctor meets\nspecified criteria.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY: New Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS: None.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE: Immediately.\n\n\n",
